      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that in 4.9 and 4.14 PIDTYPE_TGID does not exist yet and instead there is __PIDTYPE_TGID (see https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v4.9.183/source/include/linux/pid.h#L13) which is not treated as a real \"pid_type\" but instead handled in a special way inside __task_pid_nr_ns() (see: https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v4.9.183/source/kernel/pid.c#L532).\n\nWhat I can do is I can implement a similar check here like this:\n\n\trcu_read_lock();\n\tstruct task_struct *tsk \u003d pid_task(p, PIDTYPE_PID);\n\t/* Check that pid belongs to a group leader task */\n\tif (!tsk || tsk !\u003d tsk-\u003egroup_leader)\n\t\tret \u003d -EINVAL;\n\trcu_read_unlock();\n\nWDYT?",
